 "notes": "No deviation: the smoke passed first time (zero start-up offsets equal the parent exactly; probe offsets change actions on 120,904 environment-steps, none after step 60; gate reset per environment), both arms ran 24 updates on seed 5012's placements with shared direction draws, terminal means frozen before confirmation, four policies confirmed once on twelve fresh manifests (seeds 5013-5024); the smoke used two rollouts (8,201 starts; three were budgeted); 414,155 starts charged of 440,000. EARLY minus CONTINUE: +0.013 [-0.009, +0.035] (Holm p 0.49): the upper bound is below +0.05. Neither finalist improves on the frozen JOINT parent: CONTINUE -0.016 [-0.038, +0.006] (134 wins, 159 losses), EARLY -0.003 [-0.026, +0.020]; neither qualifies against the parent (both remain far above D-072). So 24 further ARS updates from JOINT give nothing, in contrast to R-118 (+0.10 from the unconverged R-116 module) and R-121 (+0.02 to +0.06): the 43-coordinate controller has plateaued under this learner at about 0.79-0.81 (JOINT here: 1,207 of 1,536 = 0.786; 0.806 in R-121's confirmation). The start-up offsets did what they were aimed at on one failure type and not on success: early drops 29 for EARLY against 42 for JOINT and CONTINUE (the first intervention since the R-106 residual to move them), with offsets up to 0.075 (thumb THJ4 +0.075, ring RFJ3 +0.060, wrist WRJ1 -0.051), but persistent-slow failures were 174 against JOINT's 158, so total success did not rise. Discordance between a continued finalist and its parent is about 0.19-0.21 here (293-321 discordant of 1,536), i.e. ARS continuation at this stage mostly reshuffles which cases succeed. One matched pair of trajectories; a single confirmation."
